17592186379380} :answer-field/id #uuid "baefd7c4-b318-5746-ace2-9ab8dd2173bf" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379379}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ba1d32c7-91d0-5ea9-ae96-737c7cf8e6a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-331052" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find $L{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ}$ given $L{f(t)}=F(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.Let $A(t)$ be the anti-derivative of $f(t)$ such that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t)$ and $A(0)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{{field-1}}\\,dτ=A(τ)\\,{|}_{0}^{t}=A(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ}=L{A(t)}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-2}}A(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's use integration by parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=A(t) & ⇒ & du={{field-3}} \\\\ dv={e}^{-st}\\,dt & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt & ={{field-4}}(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}){A}^{′}(t)\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{1}{s}A(t){e}^{-st}{|}_{0}^{\\infty }=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt={{field-5}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt.\n$$\n\nFinally, using that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt & =\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={{field-6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $A(t)$ be the anti-derivative of $f(t)$ such that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t)$ and $A(0)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ & =A(τ)\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =A(t)-A(0) \\\\  & =A(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ} & =L{A(t)}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's use integration by parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=A(t) & \\,⇒\\, & du={A}^{′}(t)\\,dt \\\\ dv={e}^{-st}\\,dt & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt & =A(t)(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}){A}^{′}(t)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A(0)=0$ and $\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ we have $-\\frac{1}{s}A(t){e}^{-st}{|}_{0}^{\\infty }=0$ and\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt=\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt.\n$$\n\nFinally, using that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt & =\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot F(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379384 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51dfecdb-ad66-5e07-8873-ca8e116b27bd" :knowledge-point/title "Proving the Formula for Laplace Transforms of Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04f4c794-b54e-52a1-a7bd-8387dc9f3dc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(τ)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379386} {:answer/id #uuid "1174f08a-d27d-5f1e-bf18-6124fe73cf05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{′}(τ)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379387} {:answer/id #uuid "82821487-e7bc-5d5f-bc8f-5c414475b01f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A(τ)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379388} {:answer/id #uuid "8f3c7730-e4a2-5af3-8513-9c1338a8bb6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A